A||N||2||RiceBurner515||Tachometer erratic - WHY???||||4||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-20-2000||10:25 PM||||I went and changed some sensors today (fan switch and O2) and when i started my car and now when i drive my tachometer bobs up and down and is erratic. When it used to idle it would steadily stay on 1000 rpm's now it jumps around in that area....ive been reading someother threads about some tach filter, what is that and what does it do? I might have touched or did something to that while looking around. What could be wrong with my tach? Carb? Spark Plug wire? Vaccuum leak? etc.......?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-20-2000||10:42 PM||||On the V6 the tach filter is to the right of the distributor.  Its a little round canister about the size of a Bic lighter.  The is a two wire clip attached to it.  They are easy to replace and, that may be the problem with your jumpy tach.  Rodny Dickman sells a replacement non stock looking tach filter that works as well.||||reg||3
Z||000002||doughboySE||11-20-2000||10:43 PM||||mine did the same pal and it ended up being the gaskets on the egr tube maybe try that?||||reg||1
